          %p W
          %h2#limits_and_colimits_in_a_preordered_set Limits and colimits in a preordered set
          %p (..)
          %h2#InFunctorCategories Limits and colimits in functor categories
          %p
            The main point is that
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits+of+functors+are+computed+objectwise"} limits of functors are computed objectwise
          %h2#ColimitOfARepresentablefunctor Colimit of a representable functor
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
            (with values in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %p
            One can readily see this from a
            = succeed "-style" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+element"} universal element
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocones"} cocones
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi D
                          %mo ,
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟵
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi D
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                              %mi C
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi C
                          %mo ,
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %mi C
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi id
                            %mi C
                            %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathcal{C}(D,C) &amp;&amp;
                  \\overset{
                  (D \overset{f}{\to}C)^\ast
                  }{\longleftarrow}
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathcal{C}(C,C)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\left\{
                  C \overset{id}{\to}C
                  \\right\}
                  }
          %p
            However, this style of reasoning does not easily generalize to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            just for definiteness of notation:
          #HodgeStarFollowedByHodgeStar.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
                over a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-truncated+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} contractible
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} small (∞,1)-category
              and consider an
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGroupoids"} ∞-groupoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Groupoids
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C}^{op} \to Groupoids_\infty
              which is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} image
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi y
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \simeq y C
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒞
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                                %mi y
                                %mphantom
                                  %mi AA
                          %mtd
                            %mi Func
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mi op
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi Groupoids
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                            %mi C
                            %mo ≔
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \&amp;
                    \\overset{
                    \\phantom{AA}
                    y
                    \\phantom{AA}
                    }{\longrightarrow}
                    \&amp;
                    Func
                    \\big(
                    \\mathcal{C}^{op},
                    Groupoids_\infty
                    \\big)
                    \\\
                    C &amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    y C
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\mathcal{C}(-,C)
                    }
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimit"} (∞,1)-colimit
              over this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
              is contractible, i.e. is the point, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} terminal object
              in
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGroupoids"} ∞Groupoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{
                    \\underset{\mathcal{C}}{\longrightarrow}
                    }{\lim}
                    (y C)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\ast
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The terminal
              = succeed "-groupoid" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
              is characterized by the fact that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Groupoids
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Groupoids_\infty
              we have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Groupoids
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo ,
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Groupoids_\infty(\ast, S) \simeq S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}\big(y C\big)
              has the same property:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Groupoids
                              %mn ∞
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %munder
                                %mi lim
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                              %mi y
                              %mi C
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mi S
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi Func
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mi op
                            %mo ,
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi Groupoids
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi y
                              %mi C
                              %mo ,
                              %mi const
                              %mi S
                              %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi const
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Groupoids_\infty
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}
                    \\big(
                    y C
                    \\big)
                    ,
                    S
                    \\right)
                    \&amp; \simeq\;
                    Func(
                    \\mathcal{C}^{op}
                    ,\,
                    Groupoids_\infty
                    )
                    \\left(
                    y C
                    ,
                    const S
                    \\right)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq\;
                    (const S)(C)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq\;
                    S
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Here the first step is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-adjunction"} (∞,1)-adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Groupoids
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi const
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %munder
